{
  "requirement": "The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet file = std::path::PathBuf::from(\"src/auth.rs\");\n```\n\nAn item within that file uses the path and selector in `OutlineData` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values. An item within a file uses the path and selector in `OutlineData`. The second obligation cites `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, so its own tests are not reassessed here.\n\n**Project-relative `PathBuf` identification**\n- `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` asserts that `list` returns `Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`. That is a root-relative path.\n- `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` checks that `list` returns relative paths such as `keep.txt` and `src/nested.txt`. It passes `read` and `parse` project-relative inputs. It asserts that `search_text` reports `matches[0].path == Path::new(\"src/nested.txt\")`. It runs with and without a git repository.\n- `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` checks that `parse` yields `id().path == Path::new(\"note.txt\")`. It also checks that `read` and `list` reject addresses that are not project-relative, namely `../outside.txt`, an absolute path and `PathBuf::from(\"../note.txt\")`.\n- `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` checks that structural matches carry the relative `node.path` (`visible.rs`, `script.py`).\n- `src/sources/tests.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` and `src/sources/tests.rs#fn[addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component]` cover provider-level addresses. They check root-relative listing, rejection of outside and absolute locations, and preservation and comparison of the address fields.\n\n**Item address as `OutlineData` path and selector**\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` asserts `parsed.id().selector == \"\"` for a file root.\n- `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` asserts `node.selector == \"fn[visible]\"` together with the relative path.\n- `tests/search.rs#fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` shows that `OutlineData::new` keeps the path and selector unchanged.\n\nThe tests cover every source tool (`list`, `read`, `parse`, `search_text`, `search_structure`). They assert both positive outcomes and rejection of non-project-relative paths. I found no gap.",
